        "original_id": "0917dbb8-21d5-5292-b45b-7aa3f43e4342",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Levinson, William Link, Bruce Geller, Joe Mannix, Gail Fisher, Peggy Fair\n- TV Series: Mannix\n- Roles: private investigator, secretary\n- Awards: Golden Globe Awards, Emmy Award\n\nFacts:\n- Bruce Bernard Geller was born on October 13, 1930, and died on May 21, 1978.\n- Bruce Geller was an American lyricist, screenwriter, director, and television producer.\n- The television series Mannix was created by Richard Levinson and William Link and developed by executive producer Bruce Geller.\n- Joe Mannix is the title character of Mannix, and Joe Mannix is a private investigator.\n- From 1968 through 1975, Gail Fisher played secretary Peggy Fair on the television detective series Mannix.\n- Gail Fisher won two Golden Globe Awards and an Emmy Award for her role as Peggy Fair on Mannix.\n- Gail Fisher was the first black woman to win either a Golden Globe Award or an Emmy Award.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "61e822d9-cadf-57dc-a4f7-72c65c529b48",
        "text": "Page: Mannix. Sentence: Created by Richard Levinson and William Link and developed by executive producer Bruce Geller, the title character, Joe Mannix, is a private investigator.\nPage: Bruce Geller. Sentence: Bruce Bernard Geller (October 13, 1930 – May 21, 1978) was an American lyricist, screenwriter, director, and television producer.\nPage: Gail Fisher. Sentence: She was best known for playing the role of secretary Peggy Fair on the television detective series \"Mannix\" from 1968 through 1975, a role for which she won two Golden Globe Awards and an Emmy Award; she was the first black woman to win either award.",
